WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.570
Between 11,000 and 5,000 years
ago, the Sahara had high rainfall,

2
00:00:05.620 --> 00:00:08.150
permanent lakes and people.

3
00:00:08.200 --> 00:00:12.330
Wet conditions reached as far
north as 31 degrees north.

4
00:00:12.380 --> 00:00:14.490
Today it is desert.

5
00:00:14.540 --> 00:00:20.350
Just to the south, the Sahel's summer
rain fell sharply in the 1970s and 1980s,

6
00:00:20.400 --> 00:00:22.410
then partly recovered.

7
00:00:22.460 --> 00:00:25.790
1984 was the driest year in the index.

8
00:00:25.840 --> 00:00:29.190
Did people turn the
Green Sahara into desert?

9
00:00:29.240 --> 00:00:30.710
Through overgrazing?

10
00:00:30.760 --> 00:00:32.010
Through war?

11
00:00:32.060 --> 00:00:34.670
In this mission, you'll
define desertification,

12
00:00:34.720 --> 00:00:40.130
and trace how cropland and overgrazing
can strip dry land of its plants.

13
00:00:40.180 --> 00:00:45.010
Then you'll judge the Great Green Wall,
which aims to restore 100 million hectares

14
00:00:45.060 --> 00:00:46.890
by 2030.

15
00:00:46.940 --> 00:00:51.640
Your mission: evaluate whether people
turned the Green Sahara into desert.
